WEBVTT

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:11.660
Brother?

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.350
You're awake?

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.080
Brother?

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.340
Brother! Brother!

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.730
In a world split into four dimensions,

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:26.410
four boys exist, all with the same face.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.170
Their dragons call to each other,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.590
almost as if seeking one another.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:11.980
Glory on the Academia!

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.050
Th-This is...

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:27.060
Damn you...

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.290
You even turned on me?

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.270
Why take out his own ally?

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:37.830
Is he...

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:45.800
They say Battle Beast turns everyone, 
whether friend or foe, to cards.

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.520
Not just the Lancers...

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.720
He even turned our five warriors into cards.

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:53.210
So he did it to the instructor, too?

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:54.990
That's really going too far!

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:58.130
No, it's as the instructor's always said.

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:00.960
On the battlefield, only the strong survive!

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:05.580
If the purpose of this is to teach 
us the intensity of a real duel,

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.930
then Instructor Sanders, who lost, 
must become a card, as well!

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:20.880
Stop it—

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:23.000
Yuya!

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:30.420
BB, you don't really want to fight, do you?

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.190
What?

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:37.130
You don't actually want to fight anyone.

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:39.100
Isn't that how you really feel?

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:41.800
Shut up! What would you understand?

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:45.400
I do understand! Because you're like me!

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:48.610
That beast of a man? Like Yuya?

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:52.300
When you built those fortresses, I realized...

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:55.580
Your fortresses are like my goggles!

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:58.990
When my goggles were down,

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:01.820
even when people laughed 
at me, or made fun of me,

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:04.760
I could pretend it was happening 
in another world.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.840
You're the same way, right?

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:09.940
Those fortresses are there to 
protect your feelings!

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:12.940
I see.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:17.190
His ferocity is that of a threatened animal.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:21.220
That's why, when Crow erased the 
jungle, he bared his fangs even more.

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:24.840
He increases his ferocity and 
shows greater power

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.540
to protect himself!

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:38.220
Yeah, that's right.

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:40.020
I don't care about orders.

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:44.780
I never wanted to be mixed up 
in the war that you started!

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:47.660
I'm gonna turn you into a card 
and escape from here!

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:48.370
No!

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:49.970
Do not interfere!

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:54.270
The instructor must become a card!

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:57.840
Through your fate, show us 
that victory is everything!

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:59.980
I believe in you, Instructor!

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:01.070
So do I.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:01.980
And I.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:03.580
Face death with honor.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.550
Glory on the Academia!

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:09.290
Glory on the Academia!

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:12.890
You people... What are you saying?

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:15.770
That's a person's life. Don't they care?

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:18.130
Are these Academia's teachings?

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:21.100
Very well...

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:22.300
Do it!

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:27.130
Even if it was a surprise attack, 
the fact is that I lost.

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:31.010
If this will teach the students the severity 
of a real battle, I do not regret it.

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:32.680
Instructor, always so noble.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:35.310
But let me tell you one thing...

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:36.480
What?

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:39.950
I had a deeper reason for this strategy.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:44.990
You were a beast, starved for battle, 
that would turn even allies into cards.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:50.200
I sent the five elites I had raised 
into this survival duel,

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:53.400
to try to produce the ultimate warrior.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.150
I thought by doing that,

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:59.000
I could fulfill the Professor's 
order to purge Yuya Sakaki.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:04.910
You are the greatest, and most evil, 
beast I have produced.

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:08.550
Turn me into a card, and use that 
power to erase Yuya Sakaki.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:10.280
You still think you can order me around?

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:12.890
This is an order from the Professor!

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:16.520
If you let Yuya Sakaki go, you won't 
make it out of here alive!

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:19.220
Won't make it out alive?

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:21.020
Let your battle soul burn.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:21.830
Survive!

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:24.560
Devour the strong, and make 
them your flesh and blood.

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:26.660
Win and stand taller than anyone else.

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:29.280
Glory on the Academia!

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:33.190
Unless I destroy Yuya Sakaki, 
I'll never make it out alive...

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:41.230
The effect of Gladiator Beast Fort.

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:44.700
One per turn, by returning a 
monster in a fort to my deck,

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:47.320
I can deal my opponent 1000 points of damage.

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:51.820
I send Augustus in the first fortress to my deck,

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:54.060
and deal damage to Yuya Sakaki.

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:55.660
Yuya has only 100 life left!

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:57.730
If he takes that 1000 damage...

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:03.670
Action Spell Acceleration!

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:06.140
I reduce effect damage to 0.

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:07.110
You won't escape!

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:12.810
I return Laquari in the second fort to my 
deck, to deal damage to Yuya Sakaki!

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:15.360
Where?

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:16.850
There must be an Action Card...

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:18.050
I activate my trap!

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:19.020
Trap?

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:20.490
Red Gazer.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:23.260
I pay half of my life

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:26.670
to negate effect damage,

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:30.680
and Special Summon one Red 
Token in defense position.

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:32.870
Thanks, Jack!

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:35.470
He damaged himself to protect Yuya.

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:38.370
Both Crow and Jack,

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:40.440
in order to protect us...

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:45.940
Damn! Damn!

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:47.310
Damn!

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:50.600
Damn BB...

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:54.070
I sent him into battle as my trump 
card. If he fails to take them out...

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:59.260
On my next turn, I will finish them.

00:07:59.650 --> 00:08:02.860
If no cards are in a Gladiator Beast fort,

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:07.230
then once per turn, I can set one 
monster from my deck in it.

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:09.930
In the first fort, I set Augustus.

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:12.640
In the second fort, I set Laquari.

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.230
I end my turn!

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:18.160
He'll turn the instructor into a card later?

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:19.580
The loser must become a card!

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:20.550
Make him a card.

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:21.510
Make him a card!

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:25.480
Make him a card! Make him a card! 
Make him a card! Make him a card!

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:27.920
Stop it! Wake up, all of you!

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:28.950
It's no use.

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:30.780
No matter how loudly you shout,

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:33.870
you cannot erase teachings that 
have permeated their minds.

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:37.430
To overturn them, you must 
shake their hearts!

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:39.400
Their hearts?

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:42.500
Listen to the cry of my soul!

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.700
My turn!

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:46.670
It's here.

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:50.880
I summon Tuner Monster Double 
Resonator from my hand.

00:08:53.210 --> 00:08:58.250
Double Resonator's effect allows me to treat 
one Red Token as a Tuner Monster.

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:00.520
Two Tuner Monsters?

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:01.950
Just like back then...

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:05.160
Listen to the beat of my soul.

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:08.930
Do you feel it? The exhilaration of my life!

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:15.260
Level 1 Red Token and Double 
Resonator Double Tune

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:18.340
Level 8 Scarlight Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:20.170
Double Tune?

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:24.550
Champion and demon, merge here and now.

00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:29.660
Touch the red dragon's soul and raise the 
cry that creates heaven and earth!

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:31.350
Synchro Summon!

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:39.800
Appear! Level 10 Tyrant 
Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:51.800
If the beast keeps howling from 
his kennel, I'll just blow it up!

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.740
Red Dragon Tyrant Archfiend's effect.

00:09:55.740 --> 00:10:00.240
Once per turn, I destroy all 
cards, except for it!

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:01.450
All cards?

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:04.700
Absolute Power Inferno!

00:10:22.210 --> 00:10:23.480
Hey, now...

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:26.120
He swept away Yuya's monsters, too!

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:29.260
Even if Pendulum Monsters 
just go to his Extra Deck,

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:30.780
it's still a heavy-handed tactic.

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:34.120
Now, he has nowhere left to hide.

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:51.460
What is this?

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:59.740
When Gladiator Beast's 
Assault Fort is destroyed,

00:10:59.740 --> 00:11:02.540
all cards on my field are destroyed,

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:06.810
and Continuous Spell Gladiator 
Beast's Great Fortress activates.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:08.680
Great Fortress?

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:12.150
So the kennel has become a stable?

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:13.710
What about BB?

00:11:13.710 --> 00:11:14.850
He's in there?

00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:17.500
When Great Fortress is activated,

00:11:17.500 --> 00:11:22.730
I can set all Gladiator Beasts 
in my graveyard within it.

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:27.900
It also negates the effect of 
monsters on both our fields.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:31.320
They say that to a coward,
 any enemy looks like a giant.

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:32.640
But I wasn't expecting this.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:36.040
It shows how afraid he's been of you, Jack.

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:38.280
Ever since that first Counter Trap.

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:40.480
Then, I'll just tear it down!

00:11:40.480 --> 00:11:42.110
Go, Tyrant!

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:43.450
Attack directly!

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:45.920
I activate Great Fortress's effect.

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:52.090
I can Special Summon one Gladiator Beast 
inside the fortress, with its effect negated,

00:11:52.090 --> 00:11:53.930
and force it to do battle!

00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:56.160
Go, Andabata!

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:58.400
When it fights, its attack points become 1000,

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:03.330
plus 1000 times the number 
of monsters in the fortress.

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:04.900
4000 attack points?

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:07.310
That's more than Tyrant's!

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:12.080
For every monster Great Fortress 
destroys and sends to the graveyard,

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:14.480
it deals 500 points of damage.

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:19.450
Combined with the 1000 points of 
battle damage, you'll be finished!

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:21.490
I activate a trap in my graveyard!

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:24.460
By banishing Red Armor in my graveyard,

00:12:24.460 --> 00:12:26.920
I prevent the destruction of a Red monster!

00:12:32.220 --> 00:12:34.220
When the Battle Phase ends,

00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:37.000
my Gladiator Beast returns to its fortress.

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:39.340
Return, Andabata!

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:42.540
Damn. I still couldn't finish him off.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:46.510
I now end my turn.

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:48.250
Are you okay, Jack?

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:52.120
Don't worry about me. Play your part!

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.250
My part?

00:12:56.160 --> 00:13:00.340
People have their own parts 
to play, just like cards.

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:03.560
My part...

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:10.060
My turn!

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:14.840
My part!

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:17.160
I understand, Jack.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:20.810
I'm gonna tear off the armor 
he's put over his heart!

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:28.720
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:34.190
Prepare to behold the fabulous world 
of the entertainment duel!

00:13:34.190 --> 00:13:35.880
An entertainment duel?

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:37.430
What's he trying to do?

00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:40.810
When there are no monsters on my field,

00:13:40.810 --> 00:13:45.640
I can activate Performapal 
Pendulum Art & Clean!

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:46.980
Behold!

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:51.590
It's repainting the field as a white canvas!

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:57.200
Then, I can Special Summon all 
Performapals in my Extra Deck,

00:13:57.200 --> 00:13:59.020
with their effects negated.

00:13:59.760 --> 00:14:04.520
Monsters summoned using 
this can attack directly.

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:08.890
In addition, I can't Special Summon 
any more monsters this turn!

00:14:11.860 --> 00:14:14.160
What's he planning—

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:18.300
He's turning a wasteland into art.

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:21.770
Now, everyone!

00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:24.640
Come back! Let's call some friends!

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:27.940
What's that?

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:30.730
You want to fight with them, too?

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:32.330
If you insist...

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:34.320
Then, come out!

00:14:34.730 --> 00:14:37.500
I summon Performapal Hid Hippo!

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:39.790
Here we go...

00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:44.530
Hid Hippo attacks BB directly, in his fortress!

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:48.630
But if he does that, BB will just 
send a Gladiator Beast out.

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:51.760
I activate Great Fortress's effect.

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:56.990
I Special Summon one monster in 
Great Fortress, effect negated,

00:14:56.990 --> 00:14:59.110
and force it to do battle!

00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:01.790
Go, Andabata!

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:04.030
Its attack points become 1000,

00:15:04.030 --> 00:15:08.520
added to 1000 times the number 
of monsters still in the fortress.

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:10.330
I thought that might happen.

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:12.860
Quick-Play Spell Performapal Guard Dance!

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:16.960
This turn, Performapals can't be destroyed,

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:19.320
and battle damage is reduced to 0!

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:23.740
This is an entertainment duel?

00:15:23.740 --> 00:15:24.900
It's so stupid.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:28.000
Now, Shieldrummer can attack directly,

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:31.290
using the effect of Art & Clean!

00:15:31.290 --> 00:15:33.280
Go on, Shieldrummer!

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:35.810
When your monster attacks,

00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:37.480
Great Fortress's effect

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:40.830
lets me Special Summon one Gladiator 
Beast and force it into battle.

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:43.220
Go, Gyzarus!

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:46.970
This one's attack points are 3000?

00:15:46.970 --> 00:15:49.830
Because there's one fewer 
monster in the fortress.

00:15:49.830 --> 00:15:52.360
The effect of Performapal Guard Dance

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:56.000
prevents Shieldrummer's destruction, 
reducing damage to 0.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:58.190
Now, let's keep it going!

00:15:58.190 --> 00:16:00.240
Go, Odd-Eyes Unicorn!

00:16:00.670 --> 00:16:05.880
Great Fortress's effect Special Summons 
Laquari and forces it into battle.

00:16:06.760 --> 00:16:11.400
But Guard Dance's effect means 
Performapals take no damage.

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:14.820
Now, Gongato attacks directly!

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:21.530
Great Fortress's effect Special Summons 
Augustus and forces it into battle.

00:16:21.820 --> 00:16:23.790
1000 attack points!

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:25.960
Which means that's the last one!

00:16:26.270 --> 00:16:30.430
Guard Dance's effect means that 
Gongato takes no damage!

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:34.270
Yeah! But Yuya still has Pararhino!

00:16:34.270 --> 00:16:37.240
There are no monsters left in his fortress!

00:16:37.750 --> 00:16:39.940
If Pararhino attacks directly...

00:16:39.940 --> 00:16:41.650
...Yuya wins!

00:16:41.650 --> 00:16:43.590
This nonsense of his...

00:16:43.590 --> 00:16:45.120
...almost has BB beaten?

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:48.010
Now, let's call out our last friend!

00:16:48.010 --> 00:16:49.560
Go, Pararhino!

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:51.090
Attack directly!

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:53.060
Yes! This will end it!

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:56.110
When my opponent attacks directly,

00:16:56.110 --> 00:17:01.230
I Special Summon Gladiator Beast Noxious 
from my hand, and force it into battle!

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:05.340
Damn it! He still had another 
monster to Special Summon?

00:17:05.590 --> 00:17:08.260
Dance, from Guard Dance's effect!

00:17:08.810 --> 00:17:11.340
I dodged all five attacks.

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:13.640
Now, there's nothing left for you to do...

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:18.280
The fun is only getting started!

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:23.650
I thought battle was over now...

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:27.060
Why aren't my monsters returning to me?

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:31.630
What's going on?

00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:35.270
What are you doing?!

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:45.380
What are you all doing?

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:48.940
Now, the other effect of 
Guard Dance in my graveyard.

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:55.350
I banish this card to swap control of the 
Performapals and your monsters!

00:17:55.640 --> 00:17:56.490
Swapped?

00:17:57.400 --> 00:17:58.560
What are you doing?

00:17:58.560 --> 00:18:00.180
Stop it... Let me go.

00:18:02.410 --> 00:18:03.560
Damn it.

00:18:04.760 --> 00:18:07.330
Don't laugh! What's so funny?

00:18:07.680 --> 00:18:10.570
You don't have to fight anymore,
unless you want to.

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:15.140
A duel isn't something anyone 
can force you to do.

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:17.510
They're for you to enjoy, for yourself.

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:21.210
Duels exist to make your opponent, 
and everyone else, smile.

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:24.420
I want to make everyone here smile.

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.380
I want you all to enjoy a real duel!

00:18:27.680 --> 00:18:28.830
Smile?

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:30.860
A real duel?

00:18:31.570 --> 00:18:34.570
As of today, stop fighting 
duels that hurt people.

00:18:34.570 --> 00:18:37.330
From now on, fight only 
the duels you want to!

00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:42.630
Now, after lots of fun, we've gotta clean up.

00:18:42.630 --> 00:18:46.240
I return Hid Hippo to my deck,

00:18:46.240 --> 00:18:50.330
to activate Performapal Pendulum 
Art & Clean's effect!

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:05.310
Wow!

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:07.260
I've never seen anything like this!

00:19:07.260 --> 00:19:09.460
This is an entertainment duel?

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:12.430
As of today, stop fighting 
duels that hurt people?

00:19:12.430 --> 00:19:16.400
This turn, I destroy all Special 
Summoned monsters!

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:24.590
Fool...

00:19:24.590 --> 00:19:28.980
If you destroy your own monsters, 
Great Fortress's effect will finish you, too!

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:32.870
Hey, haven't you learned 
anything from the lesson?

00:19:32.870 --> 00:19:38.090
Great Fortress's effect only deals damage 
for monsters sent to the graveyard.

00:19:38.090 --> 00:19:40.560
Pendulum Monsters don't go to the graveyard!

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:45.820
Pendulum is the language in 
which Yuya Sakaki speaks.

00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:49.500
Thank you for showing me another 
splendid entertainment duel!

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:54.710
Come on, BB. You're the one 
who can ultimately finish it.

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:58.940
Through Great Fortress's effect,

00:19:58.940 --> 00:20:05.990
for every monster sent to the graveyard, 
I take 500 points of damage!

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:18.240
I've hurt so many people...

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:20.860
Starting now, you can atone in lots of ways.

00:20:21.730 --> 00:20:24.100
Because you've returned to 
the person you really are.

00:20:24.430 --> 00:20:27.070
The person I really am?

00:20:27.070 --> 00:20:30.990
Yeah. And the people you 
turned into cards...

00:20:30.990 --> 00:20:32.040
I...

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:39.680
I promise... that I'll turn them back!

00:20:42.520 --> 00:20:45.400
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:20:45.400 --> 00:20:47.500
An entertainment duel?

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:51.860
You think you can escape Academia 
by getting that child on your side?

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:57.300
The next assassin the Professor has 
sent will bury you all, without fail!

00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:02.100
We'd better get going.

00:21:02.100 --> 00:21:02.970
Yeah.

00:21:03.460 --> 00:21:06.810
We need to get to Leo Akaba, 
to learn who we really are.

00:21:07.240 --> 00:21:08.810
Get going, Yuya!

00:21:08.810 --> 00:21:10.810
Save Yuzu and Serena!

00:21:10.810 --> 00:21:13.020
I promise that we'll catch up later!

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:14.460
Okay, got it!

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:15.960
I'm going on ahead!

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:17.880
I'll show you to the surface.

00:21:20.680 --> 00:21:21.690
Ruri...

00:21:22.370 --> 00:21:26.150
Stay still, Brother. I'll bring Kaito!

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:32.060
I thought this might happen.

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:37.550
I'm glad I slipped a bug into 
those musclehead students.

00:21:37.550 --> 00:21:39.610
All bugs are drawn

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:42.310
to the queen...

00:21:44.180 --> 00:21:46.540
At last, we meet again, Mr. Sakaki.

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:49.850
I won't let you leave me behind, 
like you did three years ago.

00:21:50.220 --> 00:21:54.330
I just didn't want to cause you more trouble.

00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:58.140
Academia has already become too large.

00:21:58.140 --> 00:22:00.930
If we want to destroy them, we—

00:22:00.930 --> 00:22:02.400
Destroy them?

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:04.600
Can you do that?

00:23:49.240 --> 00:23:54.000
At Academia, you were quite the 
honor student, weren't you?

00:23:54.000 --> 00:23:57.660
Knowing that, I can't wait 
to turn you into a card.

00:23:57.660 --> 00:23:59.570
I'll handle Joeri.

00:23:59.570 --> 00:24:02.030
Sir, you hurry to the Professor.

00:24:02.030 --> 00:24:04.250
I was hoping to take you all out,

00:24:04.250 --> 00:24:08.600
but I'll just have to stop you 
and then go after them.

00:24:08.600 --> 00:24:10.550
Let's get started!

00:24:11.200 --> 00:24:14.930
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
The Glorious Mechanical Dragon.

00:24:15.260 --> 00:24:17.320
The fun is only getting started!
